{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 17, :comments ["<b>In order to test you.</b> To accustom you to the prophecy to which you were privileged face to face — as was the case with Elijah, whose prophecy at that time came while he was using his senses, as it says: וַיָּלֶט פָּנָיו בְּאַדַּרְתּוֹ וַיֵּצֵא וַיַּעֲמֹד פֶּתַח הַמְּעָרָה (1 Kings 19:13) — though perhaps his was not through a luminous speculum in the manner of Moses our teacher, of whom it says: אֲשֶׁר יְדָעוֹ ה' פָּנִים אֶל פָּנִים (Deuteronomy 34:10)." "<b>Elohim has come.</b> The heavenly host, as He said above: לִקְרַאת הָאֱלֹהִים (Exodus 19:17)." "<b>And that His fear may be upon your faces.</b> As in the reply that Rabbi Yehoshua gave to the Emperor, saying: יוֹמָא דְּחַד מִן שִׁמְשֵׁי דְּקַיְימֵי קַמֵּיהּ דְּקוּדְשָׁא בְּרִיךְ הוּא, אֲמַרְתְּ לָא מָצִינָא לְאִסְתַּכְּלָא בֵּיהּ, שְׁכִינָה לֹא כָּל שֶׁכֵּן (Ḥullin 60a)."], :book :exodus, :voice :sforno, :lang :en, :chapter 20, :notes {2 "Aramaic quotation rendered as Sforno cites it from the Talmudic passage; left untranslated in keeping with the convention that quoted Hebrew/Aramaic stays in its original script."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T16:26:40.245750829Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}